.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-ENC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-enc
.Nd encapsulate a shared secret to an ML-KEM or HQC public key
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis enc
.Fl p Ar key.pub
.Fl o Ar ct
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar ss | Fl -stdout
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis enc
runs the encapsulation of the KEM named in
.Ar key.pub
with fresh randomness.
It writes the ciphertext (raw bytes, the standard's encoding) to
.Ar ct
and the 32-byte shared secret to
.Ar ss ,
created owner-only (mode 0600).
Send
.Ar ct
to the holder of the secret key; they recover the same secret with
.Xr noqtis-dec 1 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar key.pub , Fl -pub Ns = Ns Ar key.pub
A public KEM key file
.Pq Ql noqtis-key-1 ML-KEM-768 pub , No for example .
A signature key is refused.
.It Fl o Ar ct , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar ct
The ciphertext file.
.It Fl -stdout
Print the shared secret in hex (64 digits and a newline) on standard
output instead of writing
.Ar ss .
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace existing files.
.El
.Pp
The shared secret is key material: feed it to a key derivation function
or an authenticated cipher; it is not a password.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 2 on a usage error, a key that is not a public KEM key, an
existing file without
.Fl -force ,
or a file that cannot be written.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis keygen -a ML-KEM-768 -o box
ML-KEM-768 key pair: box (secret), box.pub (public)
$ noqtis enc -p box.pub -o msg.ct sender.ss
$ noqtis dec -k box -o receiver.ss msg.ct
$ cmp sender.ss receiver.ss && echo same
same
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-dec 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ,
.Xr nqenc 3
